               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 42-year-old male, admitted on 19/08/2010 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever, clinically suspicious for appendicitis. On admission, laboratory findings revealed leukocytosis with elevated CRP. Abdominal ultrasound confirmed an inflamed, non-perforated appendix. The diagnosis of acute appendicitis was established, and the patient was taken to the operating theatre on 20/08/2010, where an uncomplicated laparoscopic appendectomy was performed under general anaesthesia. The postoperative course was uneventful. The patient was mobilised early, tolerated oral intake well, and received perioperative antibiotic prophylaxis. He was discharged home on 21/08/2010 in good general condition. Please follow up wound healing and arrange removal of skin sutures in approximately 10 days. Kind regards.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
